1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[Kurapika] Chain Jail.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
An ability I will use only on the Spiders.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
CHAIN JAIL: THE RESTRAINING MIDDLE FINGER

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
A power to capture and restrain
the Phantom Troupe.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
I've sworn to use it
for no other purpose.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,000
If I break my vow…

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
if I should use this technique
on anyone other than a Spider…

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
my life is forfeit.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,000
I would die...

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,000
instantly.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
A self-imposed condition
and a contract with myself.

12
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The proof of my resolve.

13
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,000
CONDITION
CONTRACT

14
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
[theme song playing]

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
RESTRAINT x AND x VOW

16
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
[narrator] After using Chain Jail
to capture Uvogin,

17
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Kurapika and the others
flee the scene by car.

18
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
There’s a car coming up behind us.

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Can anyone confirm?

20
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
You’re right.

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Think it’s them?

22
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Looks like we’ve got a tail.
Step on it!

23
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
A tail? But how?

24
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Unless…

25
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
A thread! It’s made of Nen.

26
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Something’s attached to his left calf.

27
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Right there!

28
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Damn!

29
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
They found it.

30
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
[Feitan] Faster than expected.

31
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Don’t worry. Almost got ‘em!

32
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
[Nobunaga] Oh, whatever.

33
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Look why are we all stuffed
in this tiny car?

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
[Feitan] Just a bit longer.

35
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:11,000
MAGIC FUN CLOTH:
CONVENIENT KERCHIEF

36
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
[tires screeching]

37
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
[Nobunaga] What the hell? Hey!

38
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
-Let me out of here!
-[gasps]

39
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
You guys are no average Joes, are ya?

40
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,000
You’re fast, I’ll give you that.

41
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Fast enough to open the door
and escape in the nick of time.

42
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
I’d better stay on guard.

43
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Nobunaga was in a bad position.

44
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
[Machi] That ability of yours
is fascinating.

45
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
[Nobunaga] Let me out, dammit!

46
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
So, anything that you wrap up
in that cloth,

47
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,000
gets shrunken.

48
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
That’s the perfect accessory for theft.

49
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
With it, all of the auction merch

50
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
would fit right in his pocket.

51
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
So, he’s the one

52
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
who took all the merchandise
from the underground auction.

53
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,000
It makes perfect sense!

54
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
It also means he can turn them back
to their original size.

55
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
If I remember correctly,

56
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
the Boss said his name is Owl.

57
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Hm?

58
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Seems his friends have come to help.

59
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Yeah.

60
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
[sneering exhale]

61
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
There's more than I was expecting.

62
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Who the hell are these guys?

63
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
They can’t actually be the Phantom Troupe,
can they?

64
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
[Owl] Oh, yeah. There’s no doubt about it.

65
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
It’s just that they look so weak…

66
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,000
One, two, three...

67
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Hold on…

68
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,000
What? Is something wrong?

69
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
There are ten Shadow Beasts in all,
aren’t there?

70
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
And Uvo took care of four of them
by himself,

71
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
so... this should be all of them, right?

72
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
How odd…

73
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:18,000
The chain user grabbed Uvo
before escaping by car.

74
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,000
So, does that mean the chain user
isn’t a Shadow Beast?

75
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
[Feitan] Well, we will find out
once we ask them.

76
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Do we need to keep them alive?

77
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
[Feitan] Not all of them.

78
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
We only need the Owl.

79
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Fine. Then let me handle it.

80
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Those damn brats talking smack
like it’s no big deal.

81
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Let’s show ‘em what the Shadow Beasts
are made of.

82
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Well, you heard the man.

83
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
[Feitan] You stay there and watch

84
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
I’ll take three and Shizuku...

85
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Those two.

86
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Let’s do this!

87
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Take it easy!
Don’t underestimate their power!

88
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Oh, shut up!

89
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
[tires screeching]

90
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
[Basho] We lost them.

91
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
I think.

92
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
But for a split second,

93
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
I thought I saw someone
landing on their car.

94
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Probably the other Shadow Beasts.

95
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Let’s get back to the city.

96
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Now’s our chance.

97
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Roger that.

98
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
[Melody] We’ll switch the location
to pattern C.

99
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
And we don’t want this one
putting up a fight,

100
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
so we’ll need muscle relaxants
and sleeping gas

101
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
prepared just in case.

102
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
[Kurapika] I hope those will work.

103
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,000
One move and you’ll get cut.

104
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,000
[Owl gasping]

105
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,000
All done.

106
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
What about the bodies?

107
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Leave them.

108
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
There’s no point in hiding them now.

109
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Wow, very nice.

110
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Well, I’m thinking
maybe we should free Nobunaga

111
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
before we start torturing this guy.

112
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
-Wait a second…
-Hm?

113
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
So, then what are we doing with the Owl?
Are we gonna take the car?

114
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Let’s leave Nobunaga as is
so there’s enough room for the rest of us.

115
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
[Nobunaga] Screw that! Let me out!

116
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,000
I just don’t want to be
all cramped in there.

117
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
-[Nobunaga] Come on, you guys...
-Hey.

118
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Is there any way you can just
let the car out of the bag?

119
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
-[Nobunaga] You’re pissing me off!
-No. That’s impossible!

120
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
-[Nobunaga] Let me out!
-Too bad.

121
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,000
-I suppose it can’t be helped.
-[Nobunaga] Hey! What's going on?

122
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
You goddamn jerks!

123
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
What the hell was that, huh?

124
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[Feitan] Troupe members
don’t snap at each other.

125
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,000
You shut up!

126
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:36,000
[Feitan] Anyway, this ability
could come in handy for our job.

127
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Who cares?
I’m gonna cut this guy to shreds!

128
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[Feitan] Not yet.

129
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
First, he’s going to tell us
where the treasure is.

130
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
[Shalnark] So Feitan’s going to use
his torture skills?

131
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
You’ve got terrible luck.

132
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
[yells] Damn it!

133
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
[Dalzollene] Hey. Wake up!

134
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
I’m sure you understand
what’s happening here.

135
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:29,000
You’re going to tell us
where you hid that stolen merchandise.

136
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Does anybody know what time it is?

137
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
How long have I been asleep?

138
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Sounds like you
don’t understand the situation.

139
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
You see…

140
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
[yells] I ask the questions here!

141
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,000
[gasping]

142
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
What incredible willpower!

143
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
He knows he’s about to be tortured,

144
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
yet there’s not even
the slightest hint of apprehension

145
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
in the aura surrounding him.

146
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:15,000
His unflinching spirit is what’s behind
his seemingly invincible body,

147
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
as well as the source of his aura.

148
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
He’s the product of countless battles!

149
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
I ask the questions here!

150
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
[Kurapika] What incredible willpower!

151
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
He knows he’s about to be tortured,

152
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
yet there’s not even
the slightest hint of apprehension

153
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
in the aura surrounding him.

154
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:53,000
His unflinching spirit is what’s behind
his seemingly invincible body,

155
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
as well as the source of his aura.

156
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
He’s the product of countless battles!

157
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
[Uvogin] Can I move?

158
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
No…

159
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,000
That’s probably gonna take a while longer.

160
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
I ate dinner at about eight o’clock.

161
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
My stomach’s telling me
it’s around midnight now.

162
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[Squala gasps]

163
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Let’s make a deal, shall we?

164
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,000
[startled gasp]

165
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
You release me right now

166
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
and I’ll spare all of your lives.

167
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Huh?

168
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Hey… What is he saying?

169
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,000
He crazy or what?

170
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
-He's serious.
-[Squala] Huh?

171
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Or he seems to be.

172
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
He is? But that’s insane!

173
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
He’s the one that should be
begging for his life right now.

174
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
Now, let me make this crystal clear…

175
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,000
We’re after the auction merchandise
that was stored underground.

176
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
If you guys don’t know where it is,

177
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
then I’ve got no business with you.

178
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,000
What?

179
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
[Melody] Just wait a moment.

180
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
So, you didn’t steal all the merchandise?

181
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
The vault was empty when we got there.

182
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:14,000
I guess the Shadow Beasts
had already taken all of it.

183
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
It makes sense that
they didn’t stop to think

184
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
about telling grunts like you.

185
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
I think that he’s telling us the truth.

186
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
[Squala whines]

187
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
[Squala] Wait, then he’s serious?

188
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
So, he wasn’t bluffing
when he offered to make us a deal?

189
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
[terrified gasp]

190
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[grunting]

191
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,000
[Uvogin] Everyone makes mistakes, right?

192
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Now you know
we haven’t stolen anything yet.

193
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
So just take these things off

194
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,000
and turn a blind eye
to what we’re about to do.

195
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
If you do that…

196
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,000
then I’ll let you live.

197
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
[Kurapika] What about the guests?

198
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,000
What guests?

199
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,000
The guests who were present
in the auction hall.

200
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Our colleagues were among the crowd.

201
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Answer me.

202
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,000
I see.

203
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Really sorry to hear that.

204
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,000
They’re dead.
That was the plan from the begin--

205
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
How many people did you murder?

206
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
How many died for your selfish plan?

207
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Kurapika! Stop!

208
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Hey, knock it off!

209
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
If the merchandise is in safe hands,

210
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
we have no use for him.

211
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
We’ll just hand him over to the community.

212
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Sounds like you’re not accepting my offer.

213
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
[angry growling]

214
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Hey. Did you learn
where all the auction merchandise--

215
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
[yells] Shut up! Go ask Feitan!

216
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
[Owl inhaling deeply]

217
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,000
[Machi] Did he tell you where it is?

218
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
It was no fun at all.

219
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:26,000
I had barely gotten started
when he gave it up.

220
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Oh. So that’s it.

221
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
[Hisoka] Ah, right.

222
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
I’m supposed to meet someone today.

223
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
I’ll be leaving for a bit.

224
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
[Boss] Sure. Go ahead.

225
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
As long as you’re back
by six p.m. tomorrow.

226
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Up to no good, Hisoka?

227
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Of course, I am.

228
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Damn it.

229
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,000
[inhales, then exhales slowly]

230
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
[phone buzzes]

231
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
“Meet as promised
at the agreed-upon place.”

232
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
[Feitan] Hey, where is Shalnark?

233
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
He called in a few minutes ago.

234
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:09,000
He said that he finally succeeded
in locating a Mafia community room.

235
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
[Dalzollene] This is Dalzollene
of the Nostrade family.

236
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
We’ve captured one of the thieves
who attacked the auction

237
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
and would like to hand him over to you.

238
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,000
[mafia contact] Really?

239
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
How’d you manage that?

240
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
I’ll fill you in later.

241
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[mafia contact] Very impressive.

242
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Even the Shadow Beasts couldn’t do that.

243
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
The Shadow Beasts? Are you serious?

244
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
[mafia contact]
Yeah. In fact, they’re all dead.

245
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
[Dalzollene] All of them?

246
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
[mafia contact] Well,
where are you right now?

247
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Okay, got it.

248
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
[Dalzollene] Please. You have to hurry.

249
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
[mafia contact] Right. We’ll be sure
to bring our best people.

250
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:58,000
I gave him three canisters
of muscle relaxant gas.

251
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Understood.

252
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Some men from the community
will be here shortly.

253
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
I’ll watch over him ‘til they get here,

254
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
so everyone get some rest.

255
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[Basho and Squala] Right.

256
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Early, aren’t you?

257
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,000
[Kurapika] He’s not using In.

258
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Don’t look so worried.

259
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,000
I’ve no interest in fighting you now.

260
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Then let’s just get right to the point.

261
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
The Troupe.
Tell me everything you know about them.

262
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Oh, come now. Already?

263
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
I do just adore idle chit-chat.

264
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
[wry chuckle]

265
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,000
[Hisoka] There are 13 Spiders in all,

266
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,000
each identifiable
by their numbered spider tattoos.

267
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Members can be replaced
at a moment’s notice.

268
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:34,000
An applicant need only defeat
a current member in order to join.

269
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,000
If the Troupe loses one for other reasons,

270
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,000
it falls to the Boss to fill the vacancy.

271
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Well, to be honest,
they mainly steal and kill,

272
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,000
though they do dabble in philanthropy.

273
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
[Kurapika] That much I know already.

274
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
What you might not know already is

275
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:53,000
that I replaced number four
a couple of years ago.

276
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
[Kurapika] For what purpose?

277
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
I wanted the chance to fight the boss.

278
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
[Kurapika] The boss?

279
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:01,000
But... why would you want that?

280
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Because he’s powerful.

281
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,000
You wanted to test your strength?
That was your only reason?

282
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,000
[Hisoka] Who knows?

283
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
It… It… [moans lightly]

284
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
It just gets me so excited.

285
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Even the mere thought of fighting the boss
turns me on!

286
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
But unfortunately,
I haven’t had the chance yet.

287
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
He never lowers his guard.

288
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:31,000
He’s with at least two others
at all times.

289
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
And as soon as a job ends,

290
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,000
he vanishes...

291
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
instantly and without a trace.

292
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
So, I believe you and I
can help each other.

293
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Don’t you think our goals

294
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
are too difficult to achieve
all by ourselves?

295
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,000
[Kurapika] What are you saying?

296
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
[Hisoka] I can tell you
the Troupe members’ abilities.

297
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:02,000
There are seven whose powers
I already know about.

298
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
What do you say...

299
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
we work together?

300
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,000
[buzzer]

301
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
[Dalzollene] Yes, we’re on floor B2.

302
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
[elevator dings]

303
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
You haven’t killed him yet, have you?

304
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
No.

305
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,000
This way.

306
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
We couldn’t get a needle into him,

307
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
which meant we had to paralyze him
with gas instead.

308
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Clothes really make the man.

309
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,000
[gasps, grunts in pain]

310
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:50,000
[Dalzollene rasping]

311
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
I didn’t believe it when I heard.

312
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Never pegged you
as the type to get yourself kidnapped.

313
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
It’s time for work, Blinky.

314
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
[chuckles]

315
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:17,000
Now get in there and suck out
all the poison that’s paralyzing Uvo.

316
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
[Shizuku] Okay, all done.

317
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,000
[weary sigh]

318
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:47,000
[yells thunderously] Damn it!

319
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
I’m gonna find that chain user

320
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
and when I do, I’m gonna
make him pay for this!

321
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
Everyone! Wake up!

322
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
Where is he?!

323
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
I think he just ran away.

324
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
It’s probably because you were
so darn loud.

325
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
We’re heading back.

326
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Our job here’s done.

327
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
We took care of the Shadow Beasts.

328
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Oh, yeah! And we got the treasure, too!

329
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,000
-[Uvogin] No!
-[Shizuku and Phinks] Huh?

330
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,000
[Uvogin] You tell the Boss…

331
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,000
I’m not leaving.

332
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:30,000
I can’t go back until I settle the score
with that damn chain user!

333
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
[narrator] Uvogin has been freed
from his bonds.

334
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:41,000
And Kurapika, having just been invited
to team up with Hisoka

335
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,000
is completely unaware.

336
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
[theme song playing]

337
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[Gon] Coming up:

338
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

339
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

340
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

341
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

342
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Today, we're introducing Dalzollene!

343
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Leader of Neon’s bodyguards.

344
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Must be a real drag
taking care of that selfish brat!

345
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,000
I know, taking care of you is a real drag!

346
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,000
What are you talking about, you little--

347
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Chasing x and x Waiting."

348
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Hey, Killua! Let’s play
Drop the Handkerchief, okay?

349
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,000
I’ll drop it and you sit and wait!

350
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Killua] That’s not a two-player game,
idiot!
